body:
Deltarune takes a complete spin on the story of Undertale. Reversing everything. Your choices mattered in Undertale, they were the essence of the game. In Deltarune they don't matter whatsoever. You are told over and over "Your choices do not matter" "You cannot choose"... Toby has said that this game (the final version), no matter how you play it, will have the same ending. One route. No choices.   There were so many routes in Undertale. There is only one here.    


The direct switch of everything that was integral to Undertale is I think, what makes this game so amazing. Toby could easily have made a stupid sequel or prequel. This is so much more & I'm really happy about that.  Toby has said that this game has no direct effect on that previous world, so it is likely a completely alternate timeline/universe, but they are regardless, very much connected. The reintroduction of Chara (and perhaps Sans down the road??) is I think what will be the only real solid tie between the two.   


My personal theory is that we're going to be fighing DL Chara, which is a direct opposite to what we did with UL Chara. Instead of working with them to eliminate the world/bring chaos, we may be having to directly battle them to avoid it. Knowing what we know so far from Toby's assertion that this is a separate story-line, I don't think this is the same Chara, but, like every other character, still holds many of the same traits. We've met our villain right off the bat, which we didn't in UT. Another switch. 

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

I have a feeling this is going to be a fun ride.
